---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CTASection from '../components/react/CTASection';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Ángel Luis Catalán"
  description="Professional background and engineering approach of Ángel Luis Catalán, Senior Cloud Engineer based in Madrid."
>

  <!-- ── Header ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden border-b border-slate-800/60 py-24 sm:py-28" style="background-color: #050914;">
    {/* Grid */}
    <div
      class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 opacity-[0.04]"
      aria-hidden="true"
      style="background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(96,165,250,0.7) 1px, transparent 1px), linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(96,165,250,0.7) 1px, transparent 1px); background-size: 56px 56px; mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse at center, black 40%, transparent 75%); -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse at center, black 40%, transparent 75%);"
    />
    {/* Blobs */}
    <div
      class="pointer-events-none absolute -left-32 top-10 h-[420px] w-[420px] rounded-full opacity-25 animate-blob"
      aria-hidden="true"
      style="background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(59,130,246,0.5), transparent 70%); filter: blur(45px);"
    />
    <div
      class="pointer-events-none absolute right-0 bottom-0 h-[400px] w-[400px] rounded-full opacity-20 animate-blob"
      aria-hidden="true"
      style="background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(168,85,247,0.5), transparent 70%); filter: blur(50px); animation-delay: -6s;"
    />

    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl leading-[1.1]">
        Ángel Luis <span class="text-gradient">Catalán</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg font-medium text-slate-300">
        Senior Cloud Engineer · Azure · Terraform · DevOps
      </p>
      <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-sm text-slate-500">Madrid, Spain · Kyndryl</p>

      <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl text-base leading-8 text-slate-300">
        I've spent the last decade working in enterprise environments where reliability,
        operational discipline and scale aren't optional requirements — they're the baseline.
        That background shapes how I think about cloud infrastructure: not as a collection
        of services to provision, but as a platform that needs to be <span class="text-white font-semibold">designed,
        maintained and evolved</span>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Stats ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="border-b border-slate-800/60 py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
        {[
          { label: '10+',  desc: 'Years in enterprise environments', accent: 'from-blue-400 to-cyan-400'    },
          { label: '7',    desc: 'Active cloud & DevOps certifications', accent: 'from-violet-400 to-fuchsia-400' },
          { label: '24×7', desc: 'Critical production operations',   accent: 'from-cyan-400 to-emerald-400' },
        ].map(({ label, desc, accent }, idx) => (
          <div class={`reveal reveal-delay-${idx + 1} glass-card relative overflow-hidden rounded-2xl p-7 text-center`}>
            <p class={`text-4xl font-bold bg-gradient-to-r ${accent} bg-clip-text text-transparent`}>
              {label}
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-wider">{desc}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Professional journey ──────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="border-b border-slate-800/60 py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="reveal mb-10">
        <span class="eyebrow">Background</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold text-white sm:text-4xl">
          Professional <span class="text-gradient-static">journey</span>
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal space-y-6 text-base leading-8 text-slate-300">
        <p>
          My career started in workload automation — managing enterprise scheduling platforms
          across critical financial and industrial environments. That meant operating systems
          that ran continuously, where failures had real consequences and where documentation,
          runbooks and structured incident response were non-negotiable. Those habits didn't
          go away when I moved into cloud.
        </p>
        <p>
          Over time, the scope expanded. I moved from managing pipelines and jobs to designing
          the infrastructure those pipelines run on. First deeper into Linux systems, scripting
          and database administration. Then into cloud: Azure infrastructure, networking,
          security, CI/CD, and eventually full platform engineering with Terraform at the centre.
        </p>
        <p>
          The current role at Kyndryl is where those threads come together. Azure infrastructure
          design and deployment, Terraform automation, DevOps integration, Snowflake provisioning,
          Couchbase Capella deployment via IaC — all within enterprise delivery constraints.
          Not proof-of-concept work. <span class="text-white font-semibold">Production platforms for real clients</span>.
        </p>
        <p>
          The trajectory is clear: from operational discipline toward cloud architecture and
          platform design. The hands-on foundation makes the architectural thinking more
          grounded — I don't propose solutions I haven't had to operate.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Engineering approach ──────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="relative border-b border-slate-800/60 py-24" style="background-color: #040818;">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="reveal mb-12 max-w-2xl">
        <span class="eyebrow">Engineering approach</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold text-white sm:text-4xl">
          How I approach <span class="text-gradient-static">cloud engineering</span>
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid gap-5 lg:grid-cols-2">
        {[
          {
            title: 'Infrastructure as code is not optional',
            body:  "Manual provisioning doesn't scale and doesn't survive team changes. Every environment I work on gets a Terraform codebase — with remote state, consistent naming, modular structure and CI/CD integration from the start.",
            accent: 'from-blue-400 to-cyan-400',
            glow:   'rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.25)',
            num: '01',
          },
          {
            title: 'Automation with purpose',
            body:  "Not every process needs to be automated, but every process that runs regularly does. The goal is reducing toil and error surface, not building automation that itself becomes a maintenance burden.",
            accent: 'from-violet-400 to-fuchsia-400',
            glow:   'rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.25)',
            num: '02',
          },
          {
            title: 'Security and networking first-class',
            body:  "Azure networking is where most enterprise complexity lives: hub-spoke topologies, NSG design, Private Endpoints, DNS resolution. Retrofitting security onto an existing platform is significantly harder than designing it in.",
            accent: 'from-cyan-400 to-emerald-400',
            glow:   'rgba(34, 211, 238, 0.25)',
            num: '03',
          },
          {
            title: 'Operational clarity over clever design',
            body:  "Infrastructure that is hard to understand is infrastructure that will fail at the worst moment. Clear naming, consistent tagging, readable modules, documented runbooks — these aren't polish, they're part of the engineering.",
            accent: 'from-amber-400 to-rose-400',
            glow:   'rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.25)',
            num: '04',
          },
          {
            title: 'Platform thinking over one-off deployments',
            body:  "The most valuable infrastructure work is not delivering a single environment — it's building the patterns and tooling that make every subsequent environment cheaper, faster and more consistent to deliver.",
            accent: 'from-fuchsia-400 to-pink-400',
            glow:   'rgba(217, 70, 239, 0.25)',
            num: '05',
          },
        ].map((item, idx) => (
          <div class={`reveal reveal-delay-${Math.min(idx + 1, 5)} glass-card relative overflow-hidden rounded-2xl p-6`}>
            <span
              class={`absolute -right-2 -top-4 font-mono text-7xl font-bold bg-gradient-to-br ${item.accent} bg-clip-text text-transparent opacity-10 select-none`}
              aria-hidden="true"
            >
              {item.num}
            </span>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class={`font-mono text-xs font-bold bg-gradient-to-r ${item.accent} bg-clip-text text-transparent`}>
                {item.num}
              </span>
              <span class="h-px flex-1 bg-gradient-to-r from-slate-700 to-transparent" />
            </div>
            <h3 class="mt-3 text-base font-semibold text-white">{item.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">{item.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Focus areas ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="border-b border-slate-800/60 py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="reveal mb-12 max-w-2xl">
        <span class="eyebrow">Focus</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold text-white sm:text-4xl">
          What I <span class="text-gradient-static">focus on</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          Cuatro áreas donde dedico la mayor parte de mi energía técnica y donde
          tengo más profundidad para contribuir.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-5">
        {[
          {
            num:   '01',
            color: 'from-blue-400 to-cyan-400',
            title: 'Azure platform engineering',
            body:  'Hub-spoke topology design, VNet and subnet architecture, NSG rule management, Private Endpoints, Azure Firewall policy hierarchies, Azure Bastion, DNS zones and resolution across peered networks.',
          },
          {
            num:   '02',
            color: 'from-violet-400 to-fuchsia-400',
            title: 'Terraform and Infrastructure as Code',
            body:  'Module design, remote state with Azure Blob, workspace strategy, variable management, provider version pinning and CI/CD integration. Terraform that other engineers can read, extend and operate.',
          },
          {
            num:   '03',
            color: 'from-cyan-400 to-emerald-400',
            title: 'DevOps and CI/CD',
            body:  'Azure DevOps pipeline design, GitHub Actions workflows, service connections and OIDC-based keyless authentication, environment gating, pipeline-as-code patterns.',
          },
          {
            num:   '04',
            color: 'from-amber-400 to-rose-400',
            title: 'Reliability and operations',
            body:  'Monitoring and alerting design with Azure Monitor and Log Analytics, NSG flow logs, diagnostic settings baseline, RBAC and access governance, incident response process and runbook culture.',
          },
        ].map((f, idx) => (
          <div class={`reveal reveal-delay-${Math.min(idx + 1, 4)} glass-card flex gap-6 rounded-2xl p-6`}>
            <span class={`mt-1 font-mono text-sm font-bold bg-gradient-to-r ${f.color} bg-clip-text text-transparent flex-shrink-0`}>
              {f.num}
            </span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">{f.title}</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-400">{f.body}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Direction ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="border-b border-slate-800/60 py-20" style="background-color: #040818;">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="reveal mb-10">
        <span class="eyebrow">Direction</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold text-white sm:text-4xl">
          Where I'm <span class="text-gradient-static">heading</span>
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal space-y-6 text-base leading-8 text-slate-300">
        <p>
          The natural progression from platform engineering is cloud architecture — moving
          from implementing designs to owning them. The AZ-305 (Azure Solutions Architect Expert)
          certification reflects that direction: not a credential collected for its own sake,
          but validation of a shift in how I engage with technical problems.
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm currently building deeper expertise in Azure infrastructure, networking and
          automation, while gradually moving towards <span class="text-white font-semibold">cloud architecture
          and platform engineering responsibilities</span>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        {[
          'Cloud Architecture',
          'Azure Landing Zones',
          'Enterprise Networking',
          'Platform Engineering',
          'Internal Developer Platforms',
        ].map((tag) => (
          <span
            class="rounded-md border border-blue-500/30 bg-blue-500/10 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-blue-200 hover:border-blue-400/60 hover:bg-blue-500/20 transition-all cursor-default"
          >
            {tag}
          </span>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection />
</BaseLayout>
